From d4ee6736de1ccef9e4d071de2c80e773c6fee4a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Varun-iiitb <var3907@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 19:32:46 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 11/61] Fake liveness engine no longer opens the camera

The fake engine (debug builds only) used the real camera, and its result
carried a real camera frame as the best frame (found while taking the P5-3
screenshots). Now:
- LivenessApi starts fake sessions with no FrameSource (FakeLivenessSession
  accepts null), skips the camera-permission check for them, and sends no
  best frame for them (without a camera the fake makes up a grey frame).
- LivenessPage with useFake shows LivenessPlaceholderPreview (a grey
  silhouette, now a public widget) instead of creating a camera view, and
  does not wait for a platform view.

Checked on the S23 FE: a fake session through the Resident face gate
showed the placeholder, logged "fake engine, no camera", and left the
camera service's connect history unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../api_services/LivenessApi.java             | 47 +++++++++++--------
 lib/ui/liveness/liveness_page.dart            | 16 ++++++-
 2 files changed, 43 insertions(+), 20 deletions(-)

